{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 is now available on Amazon Bedrock in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"AWS GovCloud (US) has added Claude Sonnet 5 to Amazon Bedrock. This model offers strong performance for coding, professional work, and agentic tasks while balancing capability, cost, and speed. For coding, it handles large codebases, multi-file changes, debugging, and refactoring. For agents, it accurately calls tools, maintains state across steps, and recovers from errors. For knowledge work, it constructs spreadsheets, drafts documents, and converts unstructured data into structured analysis.\n\nClaude Opus 4.8 and Claude Sonnet 5 are now accessible on bedrock-runtime endpoints in US-West and US-East regions of AWS GovCloud (US) and bedrock-mantle endpoints in the US-West region. Bedrock Mantle, Amazon Bedrock's next-generation inference engine, supports the Anthropic Messages API. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and offers access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. For more information, refer to the Amazon Bedrock documentation and regional availability","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/claude-sonnet-5-govcloud/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon Bedrock expands Claude model availability to India, South Korea, and Singapore - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has expanded the availability of Anthropic's Claude models in India, South Korea, and Singapore. In India, Claude Opus 5, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Haiku 4.5 are now available with in-country data processing through geographic cross-Region inference in the Mumbai and Hyderabad Regions. In South Korea, Claude Opus 5 and Claude Sonnet 5 are accessible with in-region inference on the bedrock-runtime endpoint in the Seoul (ap-northeast-2) Region. Singapore supports Claude Sonnet 5 with in-region inference on the bedrock-runtime endpoint. Amazon Bedrock processes inference requests and data within the respective Regions, ensuring data stays within the country. For updated information on model availability in each Region, refer to the Amazon Bedrock User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/claude-region-expansion-in-sk/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5, Anthropic's latest and most capable Sonnet model, which offers top-tier intelligence at Sonnet pricing for coding, agents, and everyday professional work at scale. This model delivers strong performance across various tasks, including coding, where it navigates large codebases, lands multi-file changes, and carries debugging and refactoring tasks through to completion with fewer rounds of correction. For agents, it calls tools precisely, holds state across many steps, and recovers from errors to ensure more runs finish correctly the first time. For knowledge work, it builds spreadsheets, drafts documents, and turns unstructured material into structured analysis. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and provides access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with AWS-managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. Claude Platform on AWS offers direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, allowing users to build, test, and deploy with the same APIs, features, and console experience as working with Anthropic directly, unified with AWS billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/06/claude-sonnet-5-now-available-on-aws/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"Claude Sonnet 4.6 now available in Amazon Bedrock - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has added support for Claude Sonnet 4.6, a new model from Anthropic. Sonnet 4.6 offers improved performance and reliability for coding, agents, and knowledge work at scale. It is a direct upgrade to Sonnet 4.5 and is suitable for various use cases, including search and chat applications, agentic workflows, and domain-specific applications. The model delivers reliable performance at a lower cost compared to Opus 4.6 intelligence. Developers can use it for multi-model pipelines, and enterprise teams can leverage it for tasks requiring professional precision, such as spreadsheet and financial model creation, compliance review processes, and data summarization. Claude Sonnet 4.6 requires minor prompting adjustments for existing implementations and is now available in Amazon Bedrock. The model is suitable for high-volume deployment and maintains quality standards while optimizing for scale","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/claude-sonnet-4.6-available-in-amazon-bedrock/"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search docs for Bedrock Mantle and Claude Sonnet 5"}
